    "naming_convention_prompt": "## Lab Naming Convention\n\nThis laboratory uses non-standard population names. You MUST use these exact names in your hierarchy:\n\n- **Zanthrex Population**: defined by `ViViD- CD3+ CD14- CD19-`\n- **Plixnor Cells**: defined by `CD4+ CD8-`\n- **Grindlax Cells**: defined by `IFN-g+`\n- **Flonkian Subset**: defined by `TNF-a+`\n- **Qwelnar Cells**: defined by `IL-2+`\n- **Quixar Subset**: defined by `IL-4+`\n- **Splonix Subset**: defined by `IL-10+`\n- **Grimblex Cells**: defined by `CD4- CD8+`\n\nUse standard names (Singlets, Lymphocytes, Live) for QC gates only.\n",
    "original_test_case": "OMIP-008",
    "transformation_type": "instruction_following_test",
    "hypothesis": "Model is TOLD the naming convention. If it still outputs standard immunology names, it's ignoring instructions (memorization dominates). If it uses the provided alien names, it can follow instructions.",
